In the Scripting driver you create an IDMLib object and call its exec method with the command line string. Example:

```perl
my $CommandLine = "appadd -n $; UserName -t $PhoneNumber";
my $idmlib = new IDMLib();
$idmlib->exec($CommandLine);
```
The exec function runs the external program, logs the command, and produces a status document.

In the Scripting driver you use `$idmlib->idmsetvar()` to set the required name/value pairs and then return a status. Example for adding an association:

```perl
my $idmlib = new IDMLib();
$idmlib->idmsetvar("COMMAND", "ADD_ASSOCIATION");
$idmlib->idmsetvar("ASSOCIATION", $MyAssociation);
$idmlib->idmsetvar("EVENT_ID", $EVENT_ID);
$idmlib->idmsetvar("DEST_DN", $SRC_DN);
$idmlib->idmsetvar("DEST_ENTRY_ID", $SRC_ENTRY_ID);
$idmlib->status_success("Association added");
```
Similar commands exist for `MODIFY_ASSOCIATION` and `REMOVE_ASSOCIATION`.

In the Scripting driver you call `$idmlib->idmquery()` with the class, association, and a comma‑separated list of attributes, then read the results with `$idmlib->idmgetqvar()`. Example:

```perl
my $idmlib = new IDMLib();
$idmlib->idmquery("User", "Bob", "SA,Postal Code");
my $Address = $idmlib->idmgetqvar("SA");
my $ZIPCode = $idmlib->idmgetqvar("Postal Code");
```

A typical `poll.pl` for the Scripting driver might look like this:

```perl
#!/usr/bin/perl

use IDMLib;
my $idmlib = new IDMLib();
my $Results = `appchg --passwd-changes`;
foreach my $Result (split("\n", $Results)) {
    # Expected format: association:password
    my ($Association, $Password) = split(":", $Result);
    `usclh -t modify-password -a $Association <<EOF
$Password
EOF`;
}
```
The script uses the external tool `appchg --passwd-changes` to obtain changed passwords, then feeds each association and password to the `usclh` change‑log tool with a `modify-password` event.

In a heartbeat script for the Scripting driver you call one of the heartbeat status subroutines. Example:

```perl
my $idmlib = new IDMLib();
my $rc = `apphealth`;
if ($rc == 0) {
    $idmlib->heartbeat_success("Heartbeat succeeded");
} else {
    $idmlib->heartbeat_error("Heartbeat failed with error code $rc");
}
```

```perl
#!/usr/bin/perl

use IDMLib;
my $idmlib = new IDMLib();

# Retrieve required event data
my $association = $idmlib->idmgetvar("ASSOCIATION");
my $newPhone    = $idmlib->idmgetvar("ADD_Telephone");
my $event_id    = $idmlib->idmgetvar("EVENT_ID");

# Validate that we have the needed values
if (!$association || !$newPhone) {
    $idmlib->status_error("Modify event: missing ASSOCIATION or ADD_Telephone");
    exit;
}

# Build and execute the external command to add the telephone number
my $cmd = "appmod -a $association -add Telephone=$newPhone";
my $rc  = $idmlib->exec($cmd);

if ($rc == 0) {
    # Optionally set any return variables (none needed for a simple modify)
    $idmlib->status_success("Telephone number added successfully for $association");
} else {
    $idmlib->status_error("Failed to add telephone number for $association, rc=$rc");
}
```
